# Product Plan

## Do before deployment

- [ ] Add the new environment variables to the server configuration:
  - `FAST_MODEL_NAME`
  - `OPEN_LIBRARY_CONTACT_EMAIL` (recommended, not required for startup)

## Done

- [x] Route suitable suggestion work to the cheaper fast model, with main-model fallback.
- [x] Keep suggestion identity in its official original form: Persian originals in Persian and foreign works in their official English/international form.
- [x] Stop forcing title language from the interface language, Favorite-list script, or mood.
- [x] Fix poor invented Persian Movie and Book title translations by removing localization from the active flow.
- [x] Keep suggestion cards compact and omit genre/rating/publisher/album metadata; show only the work identity, creator, mood, and short reason.
- [x] Improve Book catalogue-unavailable handling with Open Library followed by strict Wikidata fallback.
- [x] Protect suggestion feedback state so rejecting/failing a suggestion cannot leave working Save/Completed controls for the wrong item.
- [x] Keep English and Persian suggestion-feedback flows structurally aligned.
- [x] Include the item name in watched/read/listened list-status confirmations.

## Closed or superseded decisions

- [x] Do not choose prompt or title language from the majority script of Favorites. Interface language controls explanatory text; verified original identity controls title and creator.
- [x] Do not force every suggestion into English. Use the original-identity rule instead.
- [x] Per-task AI routing no longer needs to wait for usage growth; it is implemented with QA visibility and safe fallback.

## Later

- [ ] After a user completes all 10 Favorites in a section, optionally send a relevant discussion invitation.
  - Not for launch.
  - Requires a frequency cap, active-room handling, join-rule safety, and no invitation Star reward.

- [ ] Explore first-time taste-label badge banners and combined profile banners.
  - Generate one banner per badge first.
  - Define how two- and three-badge combinations should work without generating an unmanageable number of assets.
  - Keep each banner first-time-only and avoid adding chat noise.

## Needs discussion

- [ ] Should Movies and Series become separate Favorites and suggestion sections?
  - This affects existing data, onboarding, profiles, matching, discussion rules, keyboards, and migration behavior.

- [ ] Should a completed Favorites list automatically trigger a discussion invitation, or should the user opt in from the completion card?

- [ ] For badge banners, should combined profiles use generated combinations, a reusable layout assembled from individual badge art, or only the strongest badge?
